{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>When your son asks you tomorrow.</b> This is the question of the wise son, from those four sons mentioned in the Haggadah. And even though it says אתכם, which implies 'to you' and not to him, nevertheless, since he says אשר צוה ה' אלהינו, he does not exclude himself from the general community, unlike the wicked son who says מה העבודה הזאת לכם. And the reason it says אתכם is because he was not yet born at the time that the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded this commandment."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:00:32.925719850Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}